INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_apRTMkSGf6dCcY', 'assistant', 'It seems I made a syntax error with the multi-line notes using `|`. I need to ensure the final closing pipe (`|`) is on its own line after the content for those notes. I also see I used map-like syntax within the `group` blocks for resources that are defined later, which might confuse the renderer''s grouping logic, so I''ll adjust the structure to define resources first and then group them.

Let''s refine the D2 structure and then compile/render.

Refined D2 Plan:
1.  Define all 10 shapes.
2.  Group them into logical clusters: **Application**, **Data Stores**, **Auth/Identity**, **LLM/AI**, **Orchestration**.
3.  Define connections based on `depends_on` and environment variable configuration.
4.  Add notes for critical configuration details.

Start by fetching the cheat sheet again for reference, although I believe the syntax correction is mostly just about the multi-line block terminator.

', 'google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025', 'openrouter', false, NULL, '[{"id": "tool_mcphub-d2____d2-fetch_d2_cheat_sheet____mcp_OkVK2fWDMGCErg2GuY8k", "type": "mcp", "apiName": "d2-fetch_d2_cheat_sheet", "arguments": "{}", "identifier": "mcphub-d2"}]', NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_2GkCyaRFCHWo', 'tpc_DFOfxmtzhkQN', 'msg_1MTWVudipNENyO', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:13:46.451196+00', '2026-04-29 10:13:48.528+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:13:46.451196+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"tps": 194.90131578947367, "ttft": 572, "latency": 1788, "duration": 1216, "totalTokens": 8720, "inputTextTokens": 8483, "outputTextTokens": 237, "totalInputTokens": 8483, "inputCachedTokens": 6987, "totalOutputTokens": 237, "inputCacheMissTokens": 1496}', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_hDmYUC87IaqDZq', 'tool', '"# D2 (Declarative Diagramming) - Comprehensive Cheat Sheet\n\n**Version:** D2 v0.7+ | **Last Updated:** October 2025\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Documentation:** [d2lang.com/tour](https://d2lang.com/tour)\n- **GitHub:** [github.com/terrastruct/d2](https://github.com/terrastruct/d2)\n- **Icon Library:** [icons.terrastruct.com](https://icons.terrastruct.com)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```d2\n# Basic connection\nhello -> world\n\n# With labels\nhello: Hi -> world: Bye\n```\n\n---\n\n## Shapes\n\n### Basic Declaration\n```d2\n# Simple shape\nserver\n\n# With label\ndb: Database\n\n# Multiple shapes on one line\nfrontend; backend; database\n```\n\n### Shape Types\n```d2\nshape: rectangle      # default\nshape: square\nshape: circle\nshape: oval\nshape: diamond\nshape: parallelogram\nshape: hexagon\nshape: octagon\nshape: triangle\nshape: cylinder\nshape: queue\nshape: page\nshape: package\nshape: cloud\nshape: callout\nshape: step\nshape: text          # standalone text\nshape: code          # code block\nshape: class         # UML class\nshape: sql_table     # database table\nshape: sequence_diagram  # sequence diagram container\n```\n\n### Dimensions\n```d2\nserver: {\n  width: 100\n  height: 200\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Connections\n\n### Connection Types\n```d2\na -- b    # undirected\na -> b    # directed\na <- b    # reverse directed\na <-> b   # bidirectional\n```\n\n### Connection Labels\n```d2\na -> b: connection label\n\n# Chained connections\na -> b -> c -> d\n```\n\n### Repeated Connections\n```d2\n# Creates multiple connections, not override\na -> b\na -> b\n```\n\n### Arrowheads\n```d2\nx -> y: {\n  source-arrowhead: triangle    # default, can be unfilled\n  target-arrowhead: arrow       # pointier triangle\n}\n\n# Available arrowheads:\n# - triangle (default)\n# - arrow\n# - diamond (unfilled or filled)\n# - circle (unfilled or filled)\n# - box (unfilled or filled)\n# - cf-one, cf-one-required (crow''s foot)\n# - cf-many, cf-many-required\n\n# Arrowhead labels\nx -> y: {\n  source-arrowhead: {\n    shape: diamond\n    label: 1\n  }\n  target-arrowhead: {\n    shape: diamond\n    label: n\n    style.filled: true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Referencing Connections\n```d2\n# First connection: (a -> b)[0]\n# Second connection: (a -> b)[1]\n(a -> b)[0].style.stroke: red\n```\n\n---\n\n## Containers\n\n### Method 1: Dot Notation\n```d2\naws.server\naws.database\n```\n\n### Method 2: Map Syntax\n```d2\naws: {\n  server\n  database\n  region: us-east-1\n}\n```\n\n### Nested Containers\n```d2\ncloud: {\n  vpc: {\n    subnet: {\n      instance\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# Connect across containers\ncloud.vpc.subnet.instance -> database\n```\n\n---\n\n## Styling\n\n### Complete Style Properties\n```d2\nshape: {\n  style: {\n    opacity: 0.5              # 0-1\n    stroke: \"#FF5733\"         # color/hex/gradient\n    fill: blue                # color/hex/gradient\n    fill-pattern: dots        # dots/lines/grain/none\n    stroke-width: 3           # 1-15\n    stroke-dash: 5            # 0-10\n    border-radius: 10         # 0-20\n    shadow: true              # true/false\n    3d: true                  # true/false (rect/square only)\n    multiple: true            # stacked effect\n    double-border: true       # double outline\n    font: mono                # mono (more coming)\n    font-size: 24             # 8-100\n    font-color: red           # color/hex\n    animated: true            # true/false\n    bold: true                # true/false\n    italic: true              # true/false\n    underline: true           # true/false\n    text-transform: uppercase # uppercase/lowercase/title/none\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Gradient Examples\n```d2\nserver: {\n  style.fill: \"#8BC34A;#0D47A1\"  # linear gradient\n}\n```\n\n### Root-Level Styles\n```d2\nstyle: {\n  fill: \"#f0f0f0\"         # diagram background\n  fill-pattern: dots      # background pattern\n  stroke: black           # frame color\n  stroke-width: 2         # frame width\n  stroke-dash: 3          # dashed frame\n  double-border: true     # double frame\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Icons & Images\n\n```d2\n# From URL\nserver: {\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Compute/EC2.svg\n}\n\n# Local file\ndatabase: {\n  icon: ./images/db-icon.png\n}\n\n# Icon positioning\nserver: {\n  icon: https://example.com/icon.png\n  icon.near: top-left\n}\n```\n\n**Icon Library:** [icons.terrastruct.com](https://icons.terrastruct.com)\n\n---\n\n## Text, Markdown & Code\n\n### Markdown\n```d2\nexplanation: |md\n  # Header\n  - List item\n  - **Bold** and *italic*\n  \n  Code: `inline code`\n|\n```\n\n### Code Blocks\n```d2\napi: |go\n  func main() {\n    fmt.Println(\"Hello D2\")\n  }\n|\n\n# Supported languages: go, py, js, rb, ts, java, c, cpp, rust, etc.\n# Full list: github.com/alecthomas/chroma\n```\n\n### LaTeX\n```d2\nformula: |latex\n  E = mc^2\n  \n  \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n|\n\n# Font sizing in LaTeX\nequation: |tex\n  \\huge{x = 5}\n  \\large{y = 10}\n|\n```\n\n### Block Strings (Multi-line)\n```d2\n# Standard\ntext: |\n  Line 1\n  Line 2\n|\n\n# Custom delimiters (for languages using |)\ncode: ||\n  if (x || y) { }\n||\n\n# Triple pipe\nscript: |||\n  // even more complex\n|||\n\n# Any special character after first pipe\ncontent: |###\n  custom delimiter\n|###\n```\n\n### Plain Text (Non-Markdown)\n```d2\nnote: {\n  shape: text\n}\nnote: This is plain text, not markdown\n```\n\n---\n\n## Special Shapes\n\n### SQL Tables\n```d2\nusers: {\n  shape: sql_table\n  \n  # Columns with constraints\n  id: int {constraint: primary_key}\n  email: varchar {constraint: unique}\n  created_at: timestamp\n  department_id: int {constraint: foreign_key}\n}\n\n# Relationships\nusers.department_id -> departments.id\n```\n\n### UML Classes\n```d2\nDatabaseManager: {\n  shape: class\n  \n  # Public (+), Private (-), Protected (#)\n  +connection: Connection\n  -poolSize: int\n  #timeout: int\n  \n  +connect(): void\n  +disconnect(): void\n  -validateConnection(): bool\n  #reconnect(): void\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Sequence Diagrams\n\n```d2\nsequence: {\n  shape: sequence_diagram\n  \n  # Define actors (optional, for ordering)\n  alice\n  bob\n  \n  # Messages\n  alice -> bob: Hello\n  bob -> alice: Hi there!\n  \n  # Self-messages\n  alice -> alice: thinking...\n  \n  # Spans (lifespans/activation boxes)\n  bob.\"critical section\": {\n    alice -> bob.\"critical section\": request\n    bob.\"critical section\" -> alice: response\n  }\n  \n  # Notes\n  alice.note: {\n    shape: text\n  }\n  alice.note: Remember to respond\n  \n  # Groups (fragments)\n  group1: {\n    alice -> bob: message in group\n  }\n  group1.label: Optional Operation\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Interactive Features\n\n### Tooltips\n```d2\nserver: {\n  tooltip: \"This is a web server running nginx\"\n}\n```\n\n### Links\n```d2\ndocs: {\n  link: https://d2lang.com\n}\n\n# With URL fragments (must quote or escape #)\npage: {\n  link: \"https://example.com/page#section\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Animations\n\n```d2\n# Animated shape\nloading: {\n  style.animated: true\n}\n\n# Animated connection\na -> b: {\n  style.animated: true\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Comments\n\n```d2\n# Single line comment\n\n# Multi-line description\n# continues here\n# and here\n\nserver # inline comment (not recommended)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Positioning & Layout\n\n### Near Keyword\n```d2\nx; y; z\n\nx.label.near: outside-top-left\ny.icon.near: top-center\nz.label.near: inside-bottom-right\n\n# Positions: \n# top-left, top-center, top-right\n# center-left, center-right\n# bottom-left, bottom-center, bottom-right\n# inside-* or outside-* variants\n```\n\n### Direction\n```d2\ndirection: right  # up/down/left/right (default: down)\n\ncontainer: {\n  direction: down  # can set per container\n  a -> b -> c\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Themes\n\n```d2\n# Available themes (100+ built-in):\n# 0: Neutral default\n# 1: Neutral grey\n# 2: Flagship terrastruct\n# 3: Cool classics\n# 4: Mixed berry blue\n# 5-7: Various professional themes\n# 8: Earth tones\n# 100-200+: Community themes\n# 300-400+: Sketch themes\n```\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Features\n\n### Globs (Pattern Matching)\n```d2\n# Style all children\n*.style.fill: blue\n\n# Nested glob\naws.*.style.stroke: red\n\n# Change defaults\n**.style.border-radius: 8\n```\n\n### Imports\n```d2\n# Import another D2 file\n...@common.d2\n\n# Import into specific scope\naws: {\n  ...@aws-resources.d2\n}\n```\n\n### Variables (Vars)\n```d2\nvars: {\n  primary-color: \"#FF5733\"\n  server-width: 150\n}\n\nserver: {\n  style.fill: ${primary-color}\n  width: ${server-width}\n}\n```\n\n### Layers & Scenarios\n```d2\nlayers: {\n  base: {\n    a -> b\n  }\n  detailed: {\n    a -> b -> c -> d\n  }\n}\n\nscenarios: {\n  normal: {\n    server.style.fill: green\n  }\n  error: {\n    server.style.fill: red\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Reserved Keywords (Quote if Using as ID)\n```d2\n\"shape\": This is okay\n\"style\": Works when quoted\n\"label\": Can be ID when quoted\n\"width\": Quote these reserved words\n\"height\"\n\"icon\"\n\"tooltip\"\n\"link\"\n\"near\"\n\"direction\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Tips & Tricks\n\n### 1. Keep Keys Case-Insensitive\n```d2\n# These reference the same shape\nPostgreSQL -> MySQL\npostgresql -> mysql\n```\n\n### 2. Use Semicolons for Compact Definitions\n```d2\nfrontend; backend; database; cache\n```\n\n### 3. Connection vs Shape Reference\n```d2\n# Creates shape first, then connects\nserver\ndatabase\nserver -> database\n\n# Or in one line\nserver -> database  # creates both if they don''t exist\n```\n\n### 4. Transparent Fill\n```d2\nbox: {\n  style.fill: transparent\n}\n```\n\n### 5. High Border-Radius for Pills\n```d2\nbutton: {\n  style.border-radius: 20\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Example: Complete Diagram\n\n```d2\ndirection: right\n\n# Root style\nstyle: {\n  fill: \"#f5f5f5\"\n  stroke: \"#333\"\n}\n\ntitle: Web Application Architecture {\n  shape: text\n  near: top-center\n  style.font-size: 32\n  style.bold: true\n}\n\n# Frontend\nfrontend: Frontend {\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/dev/react.svg\n  style.fill: \"#61DAFB\"\n  style.multiple: true\n  \n  tooltip: \"React SPA\"\n}\n\n# API Layer\napi: API Gateway {\n  shape: hexagon\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Networking%20&%20Content%20Delivery/API-Gateway.svg\n  style.fill: \"#FF9900\"\n  style.3d: true\n}\n\n# Backend Services\nbackend: Backend Services {\n  direction: down\n  style.fill: \"#00758F\"\n  \n  auth: Auth Service {\n    icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Security%2C%20Identity%2C%20&%20Compliance/AWS-Identity-and-Access-Management_IAM.svg\n  }\n  \n  users: User Service {\n    icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Compute/EC2.svg\n  }\n  \n  payments: Payment Service {\n    icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Blockchain/Amazon-Managed-Blockchain.svg\n  }\n}\n\n# Database\ndb: PostgreSQL {\n  shape: cylinder\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/dev/postgresql.svg\n  style.fill: \"#336791\"\n}\n\n# Cache\ncache: Redis Cache {\n  shape: package\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/dev/redis.svg\n  style.fill: \"#DC382D\"\n}\n\n# Connections\nfrontend -> api: HTTPS {\n  style.animated: true\n}\n\napi -> backend.auth: Authenticate\napi -> backend.users: User CRUD\napi -> backend.payments: Process Payment\n\nbackend.auth -> db\nbackend.users -> db\nbackend.payments -> db\n\nbackend.users -> cache: Cache Layer {\n  style.stroke-dash: 3\n}\n\n# Notes\nnote: |md\n  ## System Notes\n  - All services use JWT\n  - Redis for session storage\n  - PostgreSQL for persistence\n| {\n  near: bottom-right\n}\n```\n"', NULL, NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_2GkCyaRFCHWo', 'tpc_DFOfxmtzhkQN', 'msg_apRTMkSGf6dCcY', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:13:48.834271+00', '2026-04-29 10:13:49.167+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:13:48.834271+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_EmOpfFUIAH801M', 'assistant', 'This structure is much cleaner. I will now use this refined model to structure the Docker Compose layout.

I will use the following groups:
1.  **Application Layer:** `lobe-chat`, `mcphub`
2.  **Identity & Auth:** `casdoor`
3.  **Data Stores:** `postgres`, `qdrant`, `minio`
4.  **Model/Inference:** `vllm`
5.  **Integrations:** `hayhooks`, `hayhooks-mcp`

I''ll use specific shapes for the main components where possible (Cylinder for Postgres, Package for Storage/Queue).

', 'google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025', 'openrouter', false, NULL, '[{"id": "tool_mcphub-d2____d2-compile-d2____mcp_rvVz3eHSgDHuOIxf4Qye", "type": "mcp", "apiName": "d2-compile-d2", "arguments": "{\"code\":\"direction: down\\n\\ntitle: Docker Compose Stack Diagram {\\n  shape: text\\n  near: top-center\\n  style.font-size: 32\\n  style.bold: true\\n}\\n\\n# --- SHAPES ---\\n\\n# Application Layer\\nlobe-chat: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: LobeChat App\\n  style.fill: \\\"#a8e6cf\\\"\\n}\\nmcphub: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: MCP Hub\\n  style.fill: \\\"#dcedc1\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Identity & Auth\\ncasdoor: {\\n  shape: diamond\\n  label: Casdoor (Auth/SSO)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ff8b94\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Data Stores\\npostgres: {\\n  shape: cylinder\\n  label: Postgres (pgvector)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#a4c3b2\\\"\\n}\\nqdrant: {\\n  shape: queue\\n  label: Qdrant (Vector DB)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#98d8c8\\\"\\n}\\nminio: {\\n  shape: package\\n  label: MinIO (S3 Storage)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#c8e6c9\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Model/Inference\\nvllm: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: VLLM (LLM Inference)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#f2f2f2\\\"\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#333\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Hayhooks Integrations\\nhayhooks: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: Hayhooks (Standard)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ffcc5c\\\"\\n}\\nhayhooks-mcp: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: Hayhooks (MCP Mode)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ffc857\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# --- GROUPS (Containers for visual segregation) ---\\n\\ngroup: Application_Layer {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#27ae60\\\"\\n  style.stroke-dash: 2\\n  style.3d: true\\n  lobe-chat\\n  mcphub\\n \\n  # Notes on App Layer\\n  lobe-chat.note: |\\n    - Configures SSO via Casdoor\\n    - Connects to VLLM, MinIO, Postgres\\n  | {near: bottom-left}\\n  \\n  mcphub.note: |\\n    - Mounts /var/run/docker.sock\\n    - Interface for MCP tools\\n  | {near: bottom-right}\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Identity_Auth {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#e74c3c\\\"\\n  style.stroke-dash: 1\\n  casdoor\\n  \\n  casdoor.note: |\\n    - Relies on Postgres for user data\\n    - Used by LobeChat for external auth\\n  | {near: bottom}\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Data_Storage {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#3498db\\\"\\n  style.stroke-dash: 1\\n  postgres\\n  qdrant\\n  minio\\n  \\n  postgres.note: Used by Casdoor, LobeChat, Qdrant\\n}\\n\\ngroup: AI_Services {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#9b59b6\\\"\\n  style.stroke-dash: 1\\n  vllm\\n  vllm.note: GPU Optimized (CUDA)\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Integration_Adapters {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#f39c12\\\"\\n  style.stroke-dash: 1\\n  hayhooks\\n  hayhooks-mcp\\n  \\n  hayhooks.note: Standard webhook service\\n  hayhooks-mcp.note: Runs `hayhooks mcp run`\\n}\\n\\n# --- DEPENDENCIES & FLOW ---\\n\\n# 1. Identity Flow\\ncasdoor -> postgres: Reads/Writes User Data\\n\\n# 2. Core App Dependencies\\nlobe-chat -> postgres: DATABASE_URL\\nlobe-chat -> casdoor: AUTH_CASDOOR_ISSUER (SSO)\\nlobe-chat -> minio: S3_ENDPOINT\\nlobe-chat -> vllm: OpenAI Compatible API\\n\\n# 3. Vector DB Flow\\nhayhooks -> qdrant: HTTP/gRPC\\nhayhooks-mcp -> qdrant: HTTP/gRPC\\n\\n# 4. Wait Conditions (Service Health)\\nlobe-chat -> postgres: depends_on(healthy)\\nlobe-chat -> casdoor: depends_on(started)\\nlobe-chat -> minio: depends_on(healthy)\\nlobe-chat -> vllm: depends_on(healthy)\\n\\nhayhooks -> qdrant: depends_on(healthy)\\nhayhooks-mcp -> qdrant: depends_on(healthy)\\ncasdoor -> postgres: depends_on(service_healthy)\\n\\n# 5. Orchestrator/Adapters pointing to Core\\nmcphub -> vllm: (Implied: Calls LLMs/Tools)\\nmcphub -> hayhooks-mcp: (Implied: Orchestrates MCP commands)\\n\\n# Styling service connections based on role\\nlobe-chat -> casdoor: Authenticates via {\\n  target-arrowhead: {shape: diamond, style.filled: true}\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#e74c3c\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n}\\nlobe-chat -> vllm: Calls LLM {\\n  target-arrowhead: {shape: arrow}\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#9b59b6\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Data store access\\nlobe-chat -> qdrant: (via LobeChat''s vector store if configured but not explicit here, Qdrant is only used by Hayhooks in the ENV list)\\nlobe-chat -> postgres: Writes records\\n\\n# Hayhooks use of Qdrant\\nhayhooks -> qdrant: Reads/Writes Vectors\\nhayhooks-mcp -> qdrant: Reads/Writes Vectors {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#3498db\\\"\\n  style.stroke-dash: 3\\n}\\n|\\ncompile_result: ok\"}", "identifier": "mcphub-d2"}]', NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_2GkCyaRFCHWo', 'tpc_DFOfxmtzhkQN', 'msg_hDmYUC87IaqDZq', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:13:49.391996+00', '2026-04-29 10:13:55.891+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:13:49.391996+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"tps": 275.6727073036793, "ttft": 699, "latency": 6162, "duration": 5463, "totalTokens": 13846, "inputTextTokens": 12340, "outputTextTokens": 1506, "totalInputTokens": 12340, "totalOutputTokens": 1506, "inputCacheMissTokens": 12340}', NULL, NULL, NULL);
