INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_QCLEr1HlvutV6H', 'assistant', 'I must reiterate that **I do not have the capability to perform logins, including providing a username and password to connect to a remote server.**

My available tools do not include a general-purpose SSH client that accepts credentials like this. The `mcphub-ssh-exec` tool is a wrapper around an execution environment, and when it failed previously, it was due to an internal authentication check within that environment, not because I lacked a password input field.

**In summary:** I cannot connect to `10.2.0.3` with those credentials. My actions are limited to interacting with the file system context provided to me, or searching the public web.', 'google/gemma-4-E4B-it', 'vllm', false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', NULL, 'tpc_DYFfnZHgAe7l', 'msg_a7UCXvZr3QJSLG', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 07:39:01.61+00', '2026-04-29 07:39:06.62+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 07:39:01.61+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"tps": 41.74228675136116, "ttft": 1294, "latency": 4600, "duration": 3306, "totalTokens": 7870, "inputTextTokens": 7732, "outputTextTokens": 138, "totalInputTokens": 7732, "totalOutputTokens": 138}', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_BvcK1oQYoMIYBB', 'tool', '"# D2 (Declarative Diagramming) - Comprehensive Cheat Sheet\n\n**Version:** D2 v0.7+ | **Last Updated:** October 2025\n\n---\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Documentation:** [d2lang.com/tour](https://d2lang.com/tour)\n- **GitHub:** [github.com/terrastruct/d2](https://github.com/terrastruct/d2)\n- **Icon Library:** [icons.terrastruct.com](https://icons.terrastruct.com)\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```d2\n# Basic connection\nhello -> world\n\n# With labels\nhello: Hi -> world: Bye\n```\n\n---\n\n## Shapes\n\n### Basic Declaration\n```d2\n# Simple shape\nserver\n\n# With label\ndb: Database\n\n# Multiple shapes on one line\nfrontend; backend; database\n```\n\n### Shape Types\n```d2\nshape: rectangle      # default\nshape: square\nshape: circle\nshape: oval\nshape: diamond\nshape: parallelogram\nshape: hexagon\nshape: octagon\nshape: triangle\nshape: cylinder\nshape: queue\nshape: page\nshape: package\nshape: cloud\nshape: callout\nshape: step\nshape: text          # standalone text\nshape: code          # code block\nshape: class         # UML class\nshape: sql_table     # database table\nshape: sequence_diagram  # sequence diagram container\n```\n\n### Dimensions\n```d2\nserver: {\n  width: 100\n  height: 200\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Connections\n\n### Connection Types\n```d2\na -- b    # undirected\na -> b    # directed\na <- b    # reverse directed\na <-> b   # bidirectional\n```\n\n### Connection Labels\n```d2\na -> b: connection label\n\n# Chained connections\na -> b -> c -> d\n```\n\n### Repeated Connections\n```d2\n# Creates multiple connections, not override\na -> b\na -> b\n```\n\n### Arrowheads\n```d2\nx -> y: {\n  source-arrowhead: triangle    # default, can be unfilled\n  target-arrowhead: arrow       # pointier triangle\n}\n\n# Available arrowheads:\n# - triangle (default)\n# - arrow\n# - diamond (unfilled or filled)\n# - circle (unfilled or filled)\n# - box (unfilled or filled)\n# - cf-one, cf-one-required (crow''s foot)\n# - cf-many, cf-many-required\n\n# Arrowhead labels\nx -> y: {\n  source-arrowhead: {\n    shape: diamond\n    label: 1\n  }\n  target-arrowhead: {\n    shape: diamond\n    label: n\n    style.filled: true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Referencing Connections\n```d2\n# First connection: (a -> b)[0]\n# Second connection: (a -> b)[1]\n(a -> b)[0].style.stroke: red\n```\n\n---\n\n## Containers\n\n### Method 1: Dot Notation\n```d2\naws.server\naws.database\n```\n\n### Method 2: Map Syntax\n```d2\naws: {\n  server\n  database\n  region: us-east-1\n}\n```\n\n### Nested Containers\n```d2\ncloud: {\n  vpc: {\n    subnet: {\n      instance\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# Connect across containers\ncloud.vpc.subnet.instance -> database\n```\n\n---\n\n## Styling\n\n### Complete Style Properties\n```d2\nshape: {\n  style: {\n    opacity: 0.5              # 0-1\n    stroke: \"#FF5733\"         # color/hex/gradient\n    fill: blue                # color/hex/gradient\n    fill-pattern: dots        # dots/lines/grain/none\n    stroke-width: 3           # 1-15\n    stroke-dash: 5            # 0-10\n    border-radius: 10         # 0-20\n    shadow: true              # true/false\n    3d: true                  # true/false (rect/square only)\n    multiple: true            # stacked effect\n    double-border: true       # double outline\n    font: mono                # mono (more coming)\n    font-size: 24             # 8-100\n    font-color: red           # color/hex\n    animated: true            # true/false\n    bold: true                # true/false\n    italic: true              # true/false\n    underline: true           # true/false\n    text-transform: uppercase # uppercase/lowercase/title/none\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Gradient Examples\n```d2\nserver: {\n  style.fill: \"#8BC34A;#0D47A1\"  # linear gradient\n}\n```\n\n### Root-Level Styles\n```d2\nstyle: {\n  fill: \"#f0f0f0\"         # diagram background\n  fill-pattern: dots      # background pattern\n  stroke: black           # frame color\n  stroke-width: 2         # frame width\n  stroke-dash: 3          # dashed frame\n  double-border: true     # double frame\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Icons & Images\n\n```d2\n# From URL\nserver: {\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Compute/EC2.svg\n}\n\n# Local file\ndatabase: {\n  icon: ./images/db-icon.png\n}\n\n# Icon positioning\nserver: {\n  icon: https://example.com/icon.png\n  icon.near: top-left\n}\n```\n\n**Icon Library:** [icons.terrastruct.com](https://icons.terrastruct.com)\n\n---\n\n## Text, Markdown & Code\n\n### Markdown\n```d2\nexplanation: |md\n  # Header\n  - List item\n  - **Bold** and *italic*\n  \n  Code: `inline code`\n|\n```\n\n### Code Blocks\n```d2\napi: |go\n  func main() {\n    fmt.Println(\"Hello D2\")\n  }\n|\n\n# Supported languages: go, py, js, rb, ts, java, c, cpp, rust, etc.\n# Full list: github.com/alecthomas/chroma\n```\n\n### LaTeX\n```d2\nformula: |latex\n  E = mc^2\n  \n  \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n|\n\n# Font sizing in LaTeX\nequation: |tex\n  \\huge{x = 5}\n  \\large{y = 10}\n|\n```\n\n### Block Strings (Multi-line)\n```d2\n# Standard\ntext: |\n  Line 1\n  Line 2\n|\n\n# Custom delimiters (for languages using |)\ncode: ||\n  if (x || y) { }\n||\n\n# Triple pipe\nscript: |||\n  // even more complex\n|||\n\n# Any special character after first pipe\ncontent: |###\n  custom delimiter\n|###\n```\n\n### Plain Text (Non-Markdown)\n```d2\nnote: {\n  shape: text\n}\nnote: This is plain text, not markdown\n```\n\n---\n\n## Special Shapes\n\n### SQL Tables\n```d2\nusers: {\n  shape: sql_table\n  \n  # Columns with constraints\n  id: int {constraint: primary_key}\n  email: varchar {constraint: unique}\n  created_at: timestamp\n  department_id: int {constraint: foreign_key}\n}\n\n# Relationships\nusers.department_id -> departments.id\n```\n\n### UML Classes\n```d2\nDatabaseManager: {\n  shape: class\n  \n  # Public (+), Private (-), Protected (#)\n  +connection: Connection\n  -poolSize: int\n  #timeout: int\n  \n  +connect(): void\n  +disconnect(): void\n  -validateConnection(): bool\n  #reconnect(): void\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Sequence Diagrams\n\n```d2\nsequence: {\n  shape: sequence_diagram\n  \n  # Define actors (optional, for ordering)\n  alice\n  bob\n  \n  # Messages\n  alice -> bob: Hello\n  bob -> alice: Hi there!\n  \n  # Self-messages\n  alice -> alice: thinking...\n  \n  # Spans (lifespans/activation boxes)\n  bob.\"critical section\": {\n    alice -> bob.\"critical section\": request\n    bob.\"critical section\" -> alice: response\n  }\n  \n  # Notes\n  alice.note: {\n    shape: text\n  }\n  alice.note: Remember to respond\n  \n  # Groups (fragments)\n  group1: {\n    alice -> bob: message in group\n  }\n  group1.label: Optional Operation\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Interactive Features\n\n### Tooltips\n```d2\nserver: {\n  tooltip: \"This is a web server running nginx\"\n}\n```\n\n### Links\n```d2\ndocs: {\n  link: https://d2lang.com\n}\n\n# With URL fragments (must quote or escape #)\npage: {\n  link: \"https://example.com/page#section\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Animations\n\n```d2\n# Animated shape\nloading: {\n  style.animated: true\n}\n\n# Animated connection\na -> b: {\n  style.animated: true\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Comments\n\n```d2\n# Single line comment\n\n# Multi-line description\n# continues here\n# and here\n\nserver # inline comment (not recommended)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Positioning & Layout\n\n### Near Keyword\n```d2\nx; y; z\n\nx.label.near: outside-top-left\ny.icon.near: top-center\nz.label.near: inside-bottom-right\n\n# Positions: \n# top-left, top-center, top-right\n# center-left, center-right\n# bottom-left, bottom-center, bottom-right\n# inside-* or outside-* variants\n```\n\n### Direction\n```d2\ndirection: right  # up/down/left/right (default: down)\n\ncontainer: {\n  direction: down  # can set per container\n  a -> b -> c\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Themes\n\n```d2\n# Available themes (100+ built-in):\n# 0: Neutral default\n# 1: Neutral grey\n# 2: Flagship terrastruct\n# 3: Cool classics\n# 4: Mixed berry blue\n# 5-7: Various professional themes\n# 8: Earth tones\n# 100-200+: Community themes\n# 300-400+: Sketch themes\n```\n\n---\n\n## Advanced Features\n\n### Globs (Pattern Matching)\n```d2\n# Style all children\n*.style.fill: blue\n\n# Nested glob\naws.*.style.stroke: red\n\n# Change defaults\n**.style.border-radius: 8\n```\n\n### Imports\n```d2\n# Import another D2 file\n...@common.d2\n\n# Import into specific scope\naws: {\n  ...@aws-resources.d2\n}\n```\n\n### Variables (Vars)\n```d2\nvars: {\n  primary-color: \"#FF5733\"\n  server-width: 150\n}\n\nserver: {\n  style.fill: ${primary-color}\n  width: ${server-width}\n}\n```\n\n### Layers & Scenarios\n```d2\nlayers: {\n  base: {\n    a -> b\n  }\n  detailed: {\n    a -> b -> c -> d\n  }\n}\n\nscenarios: {\n  normal: {\n    server.style.fill: green\n  }\n  error: {\n    server.style.fill: red\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Reserved Keywords (Quote if Using as ID)\n```d2\n\"shape\": This is okay\n\"style\": Works when quoted\n\"label\": Can be ID when quoted\n\"width\": Quote these reserved words\n\"height\"\n\"icon\"\n\"tooltip\"\n\"link\"\n\"near\"\n\"direction\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Tips & Tricks\n\n### 1. Keep Keys Case-Insensitive\n```d2\n# These reference the same shape\nPostgreSQL -> MySQL\npostgresql -> mysql\n```\n\n### 2. Use Semicolons for Compact Definitions\n```d2\nfrontend; backend; database; cache\n```\n\n### 3. Connection vs Shape Reference\n```d2\n# Creates shape first, then connects\nserver\ndatabase\nserver -> database\n\n# Or in one line\nserver -> database  # creates both if they don''t exist\n```\n\n### 4. Transparent Fill\n```d2\nbox: {\n  style.fill: transparent\n}\n```\n\n### 5. High Border-Radius for Pills\n```d2\nbutton: {\n  style.border-radius: 20\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Example: Complete Diagram\n\n```d2\ndirection: right\n\n# Root style\nstyle: {\n  fill: \"#f5f5f5\"\n  stroke: \"#333\"\n}\n\ntitle: Web Application Architecture {\n  shape: text\n  near: top-center\n  style.font-size: 32\n  style.bold: true\n}\n\n# Frontend\nfrontend: Frontend {\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/dev/react.svg\n  style.fill: \"#61DAFB\"\n  style.multiple: true\n  \n  tooltip: \"React SPA\"\n}\n\n# API Layer\napi: API Gateway {\n  shape: hexagon\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Networking%20&%20Content%20Delivery/API-Gateway.svg\n  style.fill: \"#FF9900\"\n  style.3d: true\n}\n\n# Backend Services\nbackend: Backend Services {\n  direction: down\n  style.fill: \"#00758F\"\n  \n  auth: Auth Service {\n    icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Security%2C%20Identity%2C%20&%20Compliance/AWS-Identity-and-Access-Management_IAM.svg\n  }\n  \n  users: User Service {\n    icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Compute/EC2.svg\n  }\n  \n  payments: Payment Service {\n    icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/aws/Blockchain/Amazon-Managed-Blockchain.svg\n  }\n}\n\n# Database\ndb: PostgreSQL {\n  shape: cylinder\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/dev/postgresql.svg\n  style.fill: \"#336791\"\n}\n\n# Cache\ncache: Redis Cache {\n  shape: package\n  icon: https://icons.terrastruct.com/dev/redis.svg\n  style.fill: \"#DC382D\"\n}\n\n# Connections\nfrontend -> api: HTTPS {\n  style.animated: true\n}\n\napi -> backend.auth: Authenticate\napi -> backend.users: User CRUD\napi -> backend.payments: Process Payment\n\nbackend.auth -> db\nbackend.users -> db\nbackend.payments -> db\n\nbackend.users -> cache: Cache Layer {\n  style.stroke-dash: 3\n}\n\n# Notes\nnote: |md\n  ## System Notes\n  - All services use JWT\n  - Redis for session storage\n  - PostgreSQL for persistence\n| {\n  near: bottom-right\n}\n```\n"', NULL, NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_2GkCyaRFCHWo', 'tpc_DFOfxmtzhkQN', 'msg_a8TxCdPzGihoGn', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:14:41.142356+00', '2026-04-29 10:14:41.574+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:14:41.142356+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_FqoIVD6RVVWvYn', 'assistant', 'This confirms that the system is indeed throwing non-closure errors likely related to how it handles properties when they are used in a specific chain. Based on the cheat sheet, I will re-enable the tooltips and the complex arrow styling, but use the block string syntax `|...|` for *all* text properties (labels, tooltips) to ensure consistency, as the cheat sheet *does* show examples for block strings.

I will use the block string syntax explicitly for tooltips and labels where they are multi-line, and simple strings otherwise. The error on line 114 (`casdoor -> postgres: Auth DB Access`) suggests that even simple labels are sometimes causing issues if the line content is ambiguous. I will put `|` around every label on connections.

Let''s try to render the diagram using this highly consistent (if verbose) approach.

', 'google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025', 'openrouter', false, NULL, '[{"id": "tool_mcphub-d2____d2-render-d2____mcp_rEMCMI1eA4sdo6k2cECK", "type": "mcp", "apiName": "d2-render-d2", "arguments": "{\"code\":\"direction: down\\n\\ntitle: Docker Compose Stack Diagram {\\n  shape: text\\n  near: top-center\\n  style.font-size: 32\\n  style.bold: true\\n}\\n\\n# --- SHAPES ---\\nlobe-chat: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: LobeChat App\\n  style.fill: \\\"#a8e6cf\\\"\\n}\\nmcphub: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: MCP Hub\\n  style.fill: \\\"#dcedc1\\\"\\n}\\ncasdoor: {\\n  shape: diamond\\n  label: Casdoor (Auth/SSO)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ff8b94\\\"\\n}\\npostgres: {\\n  shape: cylinder\\n  label: Postgres (pgvector)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#a4c3b2\\\"\\n}\\nqdrant: {\\n  shape: queue\\n  label: Qdrant (Vector DB)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#98d8c8\\\"\\n}\\nminio: {\\n  shape: package\\n  label: MinIO (S3 Storage)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#c8e6c9\\\"\\n}\\nvllm: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: VLLM (LLM Inference)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#f2f2f2\\\"\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#333\\\"\\n}\\nhayhooks: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: Hayhooks (Standard)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ffcc5c\\\"\\n}\\nhayhooks-mcp: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: Hayhooks (MCP Mode)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ffc857\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# --- GROUPS ---\\ngroup: Application_Layer {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#27ae60\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  lobe-chat\\n  mcphub\\n \\n  lobe-chat.tooltip: \\\"SSO via Casdoor; Connects to VLLM, MinIO, Postgres\\\"\\n  mcphub.tooltip: \\\"Mounts docker.sock; Interface for MCP tools\\\"\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Identity_Auth {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#e74c3c\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  casdoor\\n  \\n  casdoor.tooltip: \\\"External Auth; Relies on Postgres\\\"\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Data_Storage {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#3498db\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  postgres\\n  qdrant\\n  minio\\n  \\n  postgres.tooltip: \\\"Used by Casdoor, LobeChat, Qdrant\\\"\\n}\\n\\ngroup: AI_Services {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#9b59b6\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  vllm\\n  vllm.tooltip: \\\"GPU Optimized LLM Inference\\\"\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Integration_Adapters {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#f39c12\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  hayhooks\\n  hayhooks-mcp\\n  \\n  hayhooks.tooltip: \\\"Standard webhook\\\"\\n  hayhooks-mcp.tooltip: \\\"Runs `hayhooks mcp run`\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# --- DEPENDENCIES & FLOW ---\\n\\n# Data Store Internal Dependencies\\ncasdoor -> postgres: |Auth DB Access|\\nhayhooks -> qdrant: |Vector Access|\\nhayhooks-mcp -> qdrant: |Vector Access|\\n\\n# Application Dependencies (LobeChat)\\nlobe-chat -> postgres: |DB_URL|\\nlobe-chat -> casdoor: |SSO Provider|\\nlobe-chat -> minio: |S3 Config|\\nlobe-chat -> vllm: |LLM/Embedding Endpoint|\\n\\n# Key Data/Auth Flows (Using style blocks which caused previous errors, will be plain for now)\\nlobe-chat -> casdoor: Authenticates (SSO)\\nlobe-chat -> vllm: Calls LLM\\nlobe-chat -> postgres: Stores Data\\n\\n# Orchestration/Tooling flows\\nmcphub -> hayhooks-mcp: Orchestrates MCP Tasks\\nmcphub -> vllm: Tool Execution\\n\\n# Service Dependencies (Conceptual Wait-for)\\nlobe-chat -> postgres: waits for ready\\nlobe-chat -> vllm: waits for ready\\nhayhooks -> qdrant: waits for ready\\ncasdoor -> postgres: waits for ready\\n|\\ncompile_result: ok\"}", "identifier": "mcphub-d2"}]', NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_2GkCyaRFCHWo', 'tpc_DFOfxmtzhkQN', 'msg_a8TxCdPzGihoGn', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:14:41.884216+00', '2026-04-29 10:14:46.038+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:14:41.884216+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"tps": 396.8253968253968, "ttft": 674, "latency": 3698, "duration": 3024, "totalTokens": 18992, "inputTextTokens": 17792, "outputTextTokens": 1200, "totalInputTokens": 17792, "totalOutputTokens": 1200, "inputCacheMissTokens": 17792}', NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_lmDyXJY8DXiGgs', 'tool', '{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Error: McpError: MCP error -32603: 113:24: unexpected text after DB_URL| block string. See https://d2lang.com/tour/text#advanced-block-strings.\n131:1: block string must be terminated with |"}],"isError":true}', NULL, NULL, false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_2GkCyaRFCHWo', 'tpc_DFOfxmtzhkQN', 'msg_FqoIVD6RVVWvYn', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:14:46.415817+00', '2026-04-29 10:14:46.823+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:14:46.415817+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_MdUz1MFSNLA7uo', 'assistant', 'The compiler is explicitly failing on the block string syntax usage within the connection labels. This confirms that the general connection label syntax *cannot* use the pipe `|` delimiters, despite the cheat sheet suggesting block strings are valid.

I will abandon *all* attempts at complex styling and complex labels, and use the simplest possible structure of nodes and connections that passed the initial compilation attempts (the one before I re-added tooltips and complex arrow styles). This must work to provide the diagram.

', 'google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-09-2025', 'openrouter', false, NULL, '[{"id": "tool_mcphub-d2____d2-render-d2____mcp_RSEs1Q4lemtZELBsftqW", "type": "mcp", "apiName": "d2-render-d2", "arguments": "{\"code\":\"direction: down\\n\\ntitle: Docker Compose Stack Diagram {\\n  shape: text\\n  near: top-center\\n  style.font-size: 32\\n  style.bold: true\\n}\\n\\n# --- SHAPES ---\\nlobe-chat: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: LobeChat App\\n  style.fill: \\\"#a8e6cf\\\"\\n}\\nmcphub: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: MCP Hub\\n  style.fill: \\\"#dcedc1\\\"\\n}\\ncasdoor: {\\n  shape: diamond\\n  label: Casdoor (Auth/SSO)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ff8b94\\\"\\n}\\npostgres: {\\n  shape: cylinder\\n  label: Postgres (pgvector)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#a4c3b2\\\"\\n}\\nqdrant: {\\n  shape: queue\\n  label: Qdrant (Vector DB)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#98d8c8\\\"\\n}\\nminio: {\\n  shape: package\\n  label: MinIO (S3 Storage)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#c8e6c9\\\"\\n}\\nvllm: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: VLLM (LLM Inference)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#f2f2f2\\\"\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#333\\\"\\n}\\nhayhooks: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: Hayhooks (Standard)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ffcc5c\\\"\\n}\\nhayhooks-mcp: {\\n  shape: rectangle\\n  label: Hayhooks (MCP Mode)\\n  style.fill: \\\"#ffc857\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# --- GROUPS ---\\ngroup: Application_Layer {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#27ae60\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  lobe-chat\\n  mcphub\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Identity_Auth {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#e74c3c\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  casdoor\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Data_Storage {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#3498db\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  postgres\\n  qdrant\\n  minio\\n}\\n\\ngroup: AI_Services {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#9b59b6\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  vllm\\n}\\n\\ngroup: Integration_Adapters {\\n  style.stroke: \\\"#f39c12\\\"\\n  style.stroke-width: 2\\n  hayhooks\\n  hayhooks-mcp\\n}\\n\\n# --- DEPENDENCIES & FLOW ---\\ncasdoor -> postgres: Auth DB Access\\nhayhooks -> qdrant: Vector Acces