INSERT INTO public.messages VALUES ('msg_SMwqJNrovKRGaQ', 'assistant', 'Perfect — consulting + orange is a sharp combo. Think bold confidence, innovative energy, and clarity. Here''s your logo:

```svg
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 520 150" width="520" height="150">
  <defs>
    <linearGradient id="og" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
      <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#FF9A3C"/>
      <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#FF5722"/>
    </linearGradient>
  </defs>

  <!-- Lightbulb: bulb -->
  <circle cx="68" cy="62" r="36" fill="url(#og)"/>
  <!-- Lightbulb: base segments -->
  <rect x="53" y="93" width="30" height="8" rx="2" fill="#FF5722"/>
  <rect x="57" y="101" width="22" height="7" rx="2" fill="#E84E1B"/>
  <rect x="61" y="108" width="14" height="6" rx="3" fill="#D44018"/>

  <!-- Upward arrow inside bulb (white) -->
  <line x1="68" y1="88" x2="68" y2="48" stroke="white" stroke-width="4.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  <polyline points="54,64 68,48 82,64" stroke="white" stroke-width="4.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>

  <!-- Glow rays -->
  <line x1="22" y1="62" x2="30" y2="62" stroke="#FFAA5C" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  <line x1="106" y1="62" x2="114" y2="62" stroke="#FFAA5C" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  <line x1="34" y1="34" x2="40" y2="40" stroke="#FFAA5C" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  <line x1="96" y1="34" x2="102" y2="40" stroke="#FFAA5C" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  <line x1="68" y1="18" x2="68" y2="26" stroke="#FFAA5C" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>

  <!-- Vertical divider -->
  <line x1="138" y1="30" x2="138" y2="118" stroke="#FF7733" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.4"/>

  <!-- Text: YOUNG MINDS -->
  <text x="158" y="67" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="13.5" font-weight="400" fill="#FF6B35" letter-spacing="6">YOUNG MINDS</text>

  <!-- Text: BIG IDEAS -->
  <text x="155" y="108" font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" font-size="40" font-weight="900" fill="#1C1C2E" letter-spacing="1">BIG IDEAS</text>
</svg>
```

---

**Design breakdown:**

- 💡 **Lightbulb** with an upward arrow inside — perfectly on-brand for a consulting firm (clarity, direction, growth)
- 🟠 **Orange gradient** (#FF9A3C → #FF5722) — energetic, confident, and memorable
- ✏️ **Typography contrast** — lightweight spaced *YOUNG MINDS* over heavy bold *BIG IDEAS* creates visual hierarchy and sophistication
- **Subtle divider line** adds a clean consulting-firm polish

Would you like me to adjust anything — colors, icon style, font weight, layout, or add a tagline?', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', 'anthropic', false, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '4ee2c53f-bbd1-4a47-bb39-98f018730d41', 'ssn_sSZx6Fp9Lter', 'tpc_E2TjLDCCnqnB', 'msg_QuJ4CLXMTXUxUQ', NULL, NULL, '2026-04-29 10:52:36.781717+00', '2026-04-29 10:53:22.974+00', NULL, '2026-04-29 10:52:36.781717+00', NULL, '{"content": "Great! Consulting company, orange color. Let me design a clean, professional yet energetic logo for \"Young Minds Big Ideas\" - a consulting firm.\n\nDesign concept:\n- Professional but with youthful energy\n- Orange as primary brand color (#FF6B2B or #FF8C00)\n- A lightbulb combined with an upward arrow or growth element\n- Clean sans-serif typography\n- Maybe use dark navy/charcoal as secondary color for contrast\n\nColor palette:\n- Primary: #FF6B35 (vibrant orange)\n- Secondary: #1A1A2E (deep dark navy)\n- Accent: #FFB347 (lighter orange/gold)\n\n\n- \nNow I''m thinking about the visual execution - I want the icon to feel geometric and corporate while still conveying innovation and growth. I''ll create a stylized lightbulb with angular shapes, place an upward arrow inside to suggest momentum, and pair it with clean typography where \"Young Minds\" sits lighter and \"Big Ideas\" commands attention in bold. Building the SVG logo now...\n\nWriting SVG code... I''m reconsidering the design direction entirely—moving away from the SVG code toward something more conceptually refined. A lightbulb icon feels like the right direction for a consulting firm, but I want to explore variations: maybe the bulb contains an upward arrow to symbolize growth and direction, or I could use the letter \"Y\" as a branching symbol that works both as the company''s initial and as a visual metaphor for growth and diverging paths. Let me think through which approach feels most distinctive and memorable.\n\nI''m settling on a clean, geometric lightbulb design with an orange circle background and white silhouette, keeping the interior simple with either a spark or upward arrow. For the layout, I''ll position the icon on the left side and stack the company name on the right with \"YOUNG MINDS\" in a lighter weight and \"BIG IDEAS\" bold and prominent below it. I''m planning the proportions carefully with a 500x150 viewBox to give the icon breathing room and make the text hierarchy clear.\n\nBuilding the SVG... Writing SVG elements... Finishing the SVG text styling...\n\nNow I''m refining the overall design to feel more professional and consulting-focused. I want the typography to be bold and authoritative, the color palette to feel innovative with that orange accent, and I''m thinking about adding a horizontal divider line between the two text elements to give it that polished consulting-firm aesthetic. The layout will have the lightbulb on the left, a clean vertical divider, then the stacked text with proper spacing and letter-spacing for impact.\n\nBuilding the final SVG with a simplified lightbulb shape...", "duration": 34793, "signature": ""}', NULL, '{"tps": 72.65541875664995, "ttft": 2075, "latency": 48128, "duration": 46053, "totalTokens": 9490, "totalInputTokens": 6144, "inputCachedTokens": 4684, "totalOutputTokens": 3346, "inputCacheMissTokens": 3, "inputWriteCacheTokens": 1457}', NULL, NULL, NULL);
